# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
#
# This is not hygiene, it is a fix for observed corruption. The machine building this
# repo has core.autocrlf=true, and git classifies a file as text unless it finds a NUL
# byte early in the blob. Most assets here survive that test by luck -- a GLB, a Draco
# .bin and the baked point cloud all have NULs in their first few bytes -- but
# assets/at/jungle_soil_normal.png does not, and a fresh clone smudged it from 5,952 to
# 5,996 bytes: 44 LF bytes rewritten to CRLF, i.e. a broken PNG for every clone and
# every deploy. Verified by cloning the repo into a temp dir and diffing hashes.
#
# `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff`, which disables both the eol filters and
# textual diffing.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.glb   binary
*.gltf  binary
*.bin   binary
*.drc   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.cube  binary
*.wasm  binary

# Source stays text with normalised storage. Working-copy endings are left to
# core.autocrlf so nobody's editor fights the checkout.
*.js    text
*.mjs   text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.glsl  text
*.vs    text
*.fs    text
